==Solution 3 (Solution 1 But More Condensed)==

Since it is an equiangular hexagon, each interior angle measures <imath>120</imath> degrees, and by angle chasing you can conclude that all the triangles are equilateral. Since the area formula for an equiangular triangle is <imath>s^2 \frac{\sqrt3}{4}</imath>, the side lengths of the triangles are <imath>36</imath> and <imath>16 \sqrt{3}</imath>. In the above diagram the sum of the lengths of <imath>AF</imath>, <imath>AB</imath>, and <imath>FE</imath> is <imath>36</imath> and the sum of the lengths of <imath>BC</imath>, <imath>CD</imath>, and <imath>DE</imath> is <imath>16\sqrt{3}</imath>. Since these are also the side lengths of the hexagon, the answer is <imath>36+16+3=55  (C)</imath>.

~NamyaB.

