 B & R & ? \\  
 ? & ? & ?    
\end{tabular}</math>
<math>\Longrightarrow</math>
<math>\begin{tabular}{ c c c }
 R & G & B \\ 
 B & R & G \\  
 R & G & B    
\end{tabular}</math>
<math>\Longrightarrow</math>
<math>\begin{tabular}{ c c c }
 R & G & R \\ 
 B & R & B \\  
 G & B & G    
\end{tabular}</math>
<math>\quad 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 = 12</math>

There are <math>3</math> choices for <math>R</math>, <math>2</math> choices for <math>G</math>. <math>R</math> on the down left corner can be switched with <math>B</math> on the upper right corner.

<math>(2) \quad</math><math>\begin{tabular}{ c c c }
