==Solution 7 (Simpler Casework)==
Let <imath>x</imath> be the largest card picked up on the first pass. Then <imath>1, 2, \ldots, x</imath> are picked up first and <imath>x+1, \ldots, 13</imath> second, so define
<cmath>A = \{1, 2, \ldots, x\}, \qquad B = \{x+1, \ldots, 13\}.</cmath>
Both <imath>A</imath> and <imath>B</imath> must be non-empty such that we have <imath>2</imath> passes, so <imath>1 \le x \le 12</imath>.


Replace each card by its label, <imath>A</imath> or <imath>B</imath>, giving a row of <imath>x</imath> <imath>A</imath>'s and <imath>13-x</imath> <imath>B</imath>'s. For each such row of labels, there is exactly <imath>1</imath> way to assign the numbers back onto the cards: inherently, the <imath>A</imath>-positions must read <imath>1, 2, \ldots, x</imath> from left to right and the <imath>B</imath>-positions must read <imath>x+1, \ldots, 13</imath> from left to right. So the arrangements we want correspond one-to-one with the label rows, and the number of label rows is
<cmath>\frac{13!}{x!\,(13-x)!} = \binom{13}{x},</cmath>
choosing which <imath>x</imath> of the <imath>13</imath> positions get an <imath>A</imath>. However, there is an arrangement with all the <imath>A</imath> cards in a row followed by all the <imath>B</imath> cards. Since order is fixed to be increasing, such a row reconstructs to <imath>1, 2, \ldots, 13</imath>, which takes <imath>1</imath> pass instead of <imath>2</imath>, meaning we must subtract one case per value of <imath>x</imath>, or <imath>12</imath>.


Since arrangements of <imath>A</imath> and <imath>B</imath> between different values of <imath>x</imath> are disjoint, we can sum without worrying about overcounting:
<cmath>\binom{13}{1} + \binom{13}{2} + \cdots + \binom{13}{12} - 12.</cmath>

The sum looks awfully similar to the Pascal's Triangle row-sum identity:
<cmath>\sum_{k=0}^{13}\binom{13}{k} = \binom{13}{0} + \binom{13}{1} + \ldots + \binom{13}{13} = 2^{13}</cmath>

With a little bit of wishful thinking and rearranging, we get
<cmath>
\begin{align*}
\binom{13}{0} + \binom{13}{1} + \cdots + \binom{13}{13} - \binom{13}{0} - \binom{13}{13} - 12 &= 2^{13} - \binom{13}{0} - \binom{13}{13} - 12 \\
\binom{13}{1} + \binom{13}{2} + \cdots + \binom{13}{12} - 12 &= 2^{13} - \binom{13}{0} - \binom{13}{13} - 12 \\
&= 8192 - 1 - 1 - 12 \\
&= \boxed{\textbf{(D) } 8178}.
\end{align*}
</cmath>


~ NSAoPS

